		<Param id="9" trending="false">
			<Name>ReadMe</Name>
			<Description>Read Me</Description>
			<Type>read</Type>
			<Information>
				<Subtext>Description of this example protocol.</Subtext>
			</Information>
			<Interprete>
				<RawType>other</RawType>
				<Type>string</Type>
				<LengthType>next param</LengthType>
				<DefaultValue>
					<![CDATA[
This protocol demonstrates how to expose InterApp calls from an element to other DataMiner components (other elements, automation scripts, etc.).

- The 'Custom Data' page contains example of custom parameters that can be configured via InterApp calls. By custom parameters, we mean parameters containing data fully managed on the DataMiner side (i.e. not retrieved from the any data-source). This means that when InterApp calls to manage such data comes in, we can right away validate and accept the data or not, and provide a response to the InterApp caller right away.

- The 'DataSource Data' page contains examples of data-source parameters that can be configured via InterApp calls. By data-source parameters, we mean parameters containing data retrieved from a data-source. In this case, when InterApp calls to manage such data comes in, we need to forward the data to the data-source first, wait for confirmation from the data-source that the data has been accepted, and only then provide a response to the InterApp caller. This will therefore require more logic, buffering, etc.
					]]>
				</DefaultValue>
			</Interprete>
			<Display>
				<RTDisplay>true</RTDisplay>
				<Positions>
					<Position>
						<Page>General</Page>
						<Column>0</Column>
						<Row>0</Row>
					</Position>
				</Positions>
			</Display>
			<Measurement>
				<Type lines="20">string</Type>
			</Measurement>
		</Param>
		
